/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.176 0.216 0.282 rg
39.6850393700787407 522.4079133858267596 Td
(4.1 Security Advantages) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
39.6850393700787407 508.2346850393700493 Td
(1. Zero Token Leakage: Client-side JavaScript never handles or stores Google tokens \(ID token, access token, refresh) Tj
T* (token\). Only the app's HttpOnly session cookie reaches the browser, completely neutralizing XSS-based token exfiltration) Tj
T* (attacks.) Tj
T* (2. Authorization Code Injection Mitigation: Implementing PKCE \(S256\) on a confidential client adheres to RFC 7636 and) Tj
T* (OAuth 2.1 best practices. Intercepted authorization codes cannot be exchanged without the code_verifier, which remains) Tj
T* (securely in the signed transaction cookie.) Tj
T* (3. Comprehensive CSRF & State Spoofing Defense: The 'harvest_oidc_tx' cookie cryptographically binds state and nonce) Tj
T* (parameters to the user agent. The cookie is single-use and invalidated immediately upon callback receipt, preventing replay) Tj
T* (attacks.) Tj
T* (4. Admin Account Protection: Accounts with administrative privileges \('admin' role\) cannot be linked via Google sign-in.) Tj
T* (Even if an attacker controls a Google account with an administrator's email, the backend strictly rejects linking with) Tj
T* ('google_admin_link_blocked'.) Tj
T* (5. Brute-Force & Credential Stuffing Immunity: Users created via Google OAuth have no password set in MongoDB. Our) Tj
T* (security tests verify that these accounts cannot be authenticated via the local login form with empty, null, or arbitrary) Tj
T* (passwords.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.176 0.216 0.282 rg
39.6850393700787407 289.9669685039369824 Td
(4.2 Operational & User Experience Benefits) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
39.6850393700787407 275.7937401574803289 Td
(1. Reduced Registration Friction: Farmers and buyers can onboard in seconds using their existing Google accounts without) Tj
T* (creating, remembering, or recovering complex passwords.) Tj
T* (2. Unified Session Architecture: The frontend requires zero awareness of Google-specific authentication states. Both local) Tj
T* (and Google sign-ins terminate in identical HttpOnly 'harvest_access_token' cookies and identical '/api/auth/profile' data) Tj
T* (contracts.) Tj
T* (3. Role-Based Navigation Continuity: Google sign-in honors existing role-based routing \(Admin -> /admin-finance, Farmer) Tj
T* (-> /farmer-home, Buyer -> /shop\). New users can select their intended role \('farmer' or 'buyer'\) directly on the registration) Tj
T* (page.) Tj
T* (4. Fail-Safe Development Workflow: If Google API credentials are not configured in backend/.env, the server starts up) Tj
T* (normally without throwing exceptions, ensuring teammates working on independent modules are never blocked.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 14 Tf
